---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { grantOffers } from '../lib/grants';

const siteOrigin = Astro.site ?? new URL('https://www.wellridgegroup.com');
const siteURL = siteOrigin.toString().replace(/\/$/, '');
const offerSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Service',
  name: 'Bounded grant-writing support',
  provider: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Wellridge Group', url: siteURL },
  serviceType: 'Grant application review, letters of inquiry, and short foundation applications',
  areaServed: { '@type': 'Country', name: 'United States' },
  offers: grantOffers.map((offer) => ({ '@type': 'Offer', name: offer.name, price: offer.price.replace('$', ''), priceCurrency: 'USD', url: `${siteURL}${offer.servicePath ?? '/grant-writing'}` })),
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Grant Writing Services for Small Nonprofits Nationwide"
  description="One-time nonprofit grant support across the United States: $295 proposal review, $350 LOI writing, or a $750 short foundation application. No retainer required."
  structuredData={offerSchema}
>
  <section class="py-20 bg-gradient-to-b from-white to-fog">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-ridge-blue">A defined starting point</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-serif font-bold text-slate-deep mt-3 mb-6">Grant writing services for small nonprofits nationwide</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-600">Get help with the grant task in front of you: reviewing an existing proposal, writing a letter of inquiry, or preparing one short foundation application. Work remotely with Wellridge from anywhere in the United States, with a fixed fee and no retainer required.</p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-gray-600">Start with one identified funder and your approved program and budget. We check the instructions and agree on scope before payment. Your organization approves the facts and submits the final materials.</p>
      <a href="/contact?service=grant-writing" class="inline-block mt-8 px-8 py-3 bg-ridge-blue text-white rounded-md text-lg font-medium">Discuss your grant</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        {grantOffers.map((offer) => (
          <article class="border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-6">
            <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-ridge-blue">{offer.price} · {offer.payment}</p>
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-bold text-slate-deep mt-2 mb-3">{offer.name}</h2>
            <p class="text-gray-700">{offer.description}</p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 mt-4 text-sm text-gray-700 space-y-1">
              {offer.deliverables.map((deliverable) => <li>{deliverable}</li>)}
            </ul>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mt-4">{offer.timing}</p>
            {offer.servicePath && <p class="mt-4"><a class="text-ridge-blue underline" href={offer.servicePath}>Explore {offer.shortName.toLowerCase()}</a></p>}
            <a class="inline-block mt-5 text-ridge-blue underline" href={`/contact?service=grant-writing&package=${offer.id}`}>Discuss this scope</a>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 bg-fog">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-serif font-bold text-slate-deep mb-6">What stays with the client</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-3 text-gray-700">
        <li>The client confirms facts, approves the final materials, and submits the application.</li>
        <li>There is no award guarantee, percentage fee, federal application, new program design, or complex budget creation.</li>
        <li>Work does not begin until instructions and scope fit are inspected and agreed.</li>
        <li>Late inputs move the working deadline. Once work begins, earned work is payable; any unused prepaid scope is handled in the written engagement terms.</li>
        <li>There is no automatic recurring commitment. Additional work requires a separately agreed quote.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="mt-8 border border-ridge-blue rounded-lg p-6 bg-blue-50"><h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-bold text-slate-deep mb-2">See the review in practice</h2><p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">The fictional Northside Arts Workshop example shows how a vague draft becomes a specific, budget-consistent narrative with unresolved inputs called out.</p><a class="inline-block px-5 py-3 bg-ridge-blue text-white rounded-md font-medium" href="/work-examples/grant-review">View the fictional grant review example</a></div>
      <p class="mt-8 text-gray-700">Use the <a class="text-ridge-blue underline" href="/resources/grant-application-checklist">grant application checklist</a> before an inquiry. Compare <a class="text-ridge-blue underline" href="/resources/grant-review-loi-or-application">grant review, LOI, and application options</a>, or read the <a class="text-ridge-blue underline" href="/work-examples/letter-of-inquiry">fictional letter-of-inquiry example</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-serif font-bold text-slate-deep mb-8">Questions organizations usually ask</h2>
      <div class="space-y-6">
        <div><h3 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold">Can we hire you for just one grant?</h3><p class="text-gray-700 mt-2">Yes. Each offer covers one defined assignment without a monthly retainer. If you already have a draft, choose <a href="/grant-application-review" class="text-ridge-blue underline">proposal review and editing</a>. If you need a narrative written from approved materials, compare <a href="/letter-of-inquiry-writing" class="text-ridge-blue underline">LOI writing</a> and <a href="/foundation-grant-writing" class="text-ridge-blue underline">one-time foundation application writing</a>.</p></div>
        <div><h3 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold">Do you work with nonprofits outside Texas?</h3><p class="text-gray-700 mt-2">Yes. These grant services are available remotely throughout the United States, including Arlington, Dallas–Fort Worth, and the rest of Texas. We agree on the materials handoff, deadline and time zone, and one person at your organization who can consolidate feedback and approve facts.</p></div>
        <div><h3 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold">What if we have not found a grant yet?</h3><p class="text-gray-700 mt-2">These fixed-fee packages start with an identified opportunity. Funder prospect research is a different assignment. See the <a href="/services" class="text-ridge-blue underline">funding pipeline research scope</a> before paying for writing.</p></div>
        <div><h3 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold">Can you write to any funder?</h3><p class="text-gray-700 mt-2">The offer begins with one identified opportunity and its controlling instructions. Fit and access are checked before acceptance.</p></div>
        <div><h3 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold">Do you submit on our behalf?</h3><p class="text-gray-700 mt-2">No. The client owns final factual approval and submission authority.</p></div>
        <div><h3 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold">What if the scope grows?</h3><p class="text-gray-700 mt-2">Expansion, additional funders, new program design, or complex budget work receives a separate quote.</p></div>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-8 text-gray-700">Felix Torres leads Wellridge's opportunity judgment, narrative architecture, and final quality control. Read <a href="/about" class="text-ridge-blue underline">about Felix and the Wellridge approach</a>, then use the <a href="/resources/grant-application-checklist" class="text-ridge-blue underline">materials checklist</a> to prepare for a scope discussion.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
